// Tests for \note and \warning admonition commands, including inline commands
// (\c, \b, etc.) spanning command boundaries. Verifies that:
//  - Full text spanning inline-command boundaries is captured.
//  - Prose rules fire exactly once (no duplicate alerts from the catch-all pass).

// ─── \note with inline commands ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// SHOULD WARN: Microsoft.Passive — passive voice inside \note.

/*!
    \class QFile
    \brief Provides an interface for reading and writing files.

    Open the file before reading from it.

    \note The file is opened in text mode by default on \macos. Call \c{setTextModeEnabled(false)}
    to switch to \nullptr binary mode.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: Microsoft.We — fires exactly once inside \note.
// (Verifies no duplicate alert from the catch-all text pass.)

/*!
    \class QDir
    \brief Provides access to directory structures and their contents.

    Use this class to navigate the file system.

    \note We recommend using \c{QDir::separator()} instead of hard-coded slash
    characters to keep code portable.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: Microsoft.Wordiness — wordy phrase inside \note with inline commands.

/*!
    \class QTimer
    \brief Provides repetitive and single-shot timers.

    Connect the \c{timeout()} signal to a slot to receive notifications.

    \note Utilize \c{setSingleShot(true)} in order to schedule a one-time callback.
*/

// SHOULD NOT produce false positives: \note followed by a macro after blank line.
// Verifies collectCommandText stops at \n\n and does not consume the \QUL macro text.

/*!
    \class QTextStream
    \brief Provides a convenient interface for reading and writing text.

    \note Always set the codec before reading data from the stream.

    \QUL maintains source compatibility between minor releases.
    However, some changes may require you to adapt the application code
    accordingly.
*/

// ─── \warning with inline commands ───────────────────────────────────────────

// SHOULD WARN: Microsoft.Passive — passive voice inside \warning.

/*!
    \class QMutex
    \brief Provides access serialization between threads.

    Lock the mutex before accessing shared data.

    \warning Calling \c{lock()} from a thread on \PLATFORM1 that already holds the lock will cause
    a deadlock. Use \c{QMutexLocker} instead; it is automatically unlocked on \QtMinorVersion when
    the scope exits.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: Microsoft.We — fires exactly once inside \warning.

/*!
    \class QThread
    \brief Manages a thread of execution.

    Subclass QThread to implement custom thread logic.

    \warning We strongly advise against calling \c{quit()} on a thread that is
    still executing user code, as this may leave resources unreleased.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: Microsoft.Wordiness — wordy phrase inside \warning with inline commands.

/*!
    \class QSemaphore
    \brief Provides a general counting semaphore.

    Use acquire() to wait for a resource.

    \warning Do not call \c{acquire()} in order to block the main thread, as this
    will freeze the UI. Utilize a worker thread instead.
*/

// SHOULD NOT produce false positives: \warning followed by a macro after blank line.
// Verifies collectCommandText stops at \n\n and does not consume the \BUILDVAR macro text.

/*!
    \class QBuffer
    \brief Provides a QIODevice interface for a QByteArray.

    \warning Do not write to the buffer while reading from it.

    \BUILDVAR provides the current build configuration accordingly.
    Use \c{QBuffer::data()} to retrieve the contents.
*/
